{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2314 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "8b63b259a8b5cc3e1812da96e7a40064474753356a8cdd383631f468dac69f3f" :edb/db-before-t 2313 :edb/db-after-t 2314 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535626 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:53:45.286Z" 13194139535626 true] [17592186068615 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358186 13194139535626 true] [17592186259427 1017 #edb/ref 17592186274631 13194139535626 false] [17592186259427 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358193 13194139535626 true] [17592186259427 1145 "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{4\\sqrt{x+4}-x-8}{{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[4\\sqrt{x+4}-x-8]}^{'}}{[{x}^{2}]^{'}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x+4}}-1]}{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{4\\sqrt{x+4}-x-8}{{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x+4}}-1]}{2x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x+4}}-1]}^{'}}{[2x]^{'}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[-\\frac{1}{(x+4)\\sqrt{x+4}}]}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{[-\\frac{1}{(0+4)\\sqrt{0+4}}]}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{[-\\frac{1}{4(2)}]}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535626 false] [17592186259427 1145 "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{4\\sqrt{x+4}-x-8}{{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[4\\sqrt{x+4}-x-8]}^{′}}{[{x}^{2}]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x+4}}-1]}{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{4\\sqrt{x+4}-x-8}{{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x+4}}-1]}{2x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x+4}}-1]}^{′}}{[2x]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[-\\frac{1}{(x+4)\\sqrt{x+4}}]}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{[-\\frac{1}{(0+4)\\sqrt{0+4}}]}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{[-\\frac{1}{4(2)}]}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535626 true] [17592186358186 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358187 13194139535626 true] [17592186358186 1089 "q-115516" 13194139535626 true] [17592186358186 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535626 true] [17592186358186 1100 "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x}{x}.$" 13194139535626 true] [17592186358186 1113 #uuid "3bec609f-956f-5b26-89c0-bf155d1eac55" 13194139535626 true] [17592186358186 1145 "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x=\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }x=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x}{x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x]^{′}}{{[x]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x})}{1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535626 true] [17592186358187 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358188 13194139535626 true] [17592186358187 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358189 13194139535626 true] [17592186358187 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358190 13194139535626 true] [17592186358187 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358191 13194139535626 true] [17592186358187 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358192 13194139535626 true] [17592186358187 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535626 true] [17592186358187 1041 "selection" 13194139535626 true] [17592186358187 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358192 13194139535626 true] [17592186358187 1110 #uuid "40f8f6ec-e089-5dc6-9ad5-f319a4be13f8" 13194139535626 true] [17592186358188 1034 "\\infty " 13194139535626 true] [17592186358188 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1319413953